{
    # The evaluator's own model only reads tool output and writes it up, so it
    # is the cheap rung. Which provider depends on which key is present, in
    # neuro-san-studio's order: an entry whose key is missing is skipped. The
    # networks it measures run on the provider esp.config chooses, whatever
    # this one lands on.
    "llm_config": {
        "fallbacks": [
            {"model_name": "gpt-5.4-mini"},
            {"model_name": "claude-haiku"},
            {"model_name": "gemini-3.5-flash-lite"},
        ],
    },

    "metadata": {
        "description": "Measures neuro-san agent networks on the same questions and compares them: accuracy, unfinished runs, tokens, and which networks nothing else beats. Every call it makes to a measured network is paid for.",
        "tags": ["evaluation", "measurement", "benchmark"],
        "sample_queries": [
            "Which networks can you measure?",
            "Measure the designer's shape against the best evolved network on the built-in benchmark.",
            "Is the best-measured network still the best? Measure the top two again.",
        ],
    },

    # One measurement of four networks on seventeen questions is sixty-eight
    # multi-hop runs; the session has to outlive it.
    "max_steps": 20,
    "max_execution_seconds": 3600,

    "tools": [
        {
            "name": "Evaluator",
            "function": {
                "description": "Measures agent networks on a set of questions and compares them.",
            },
            "instructions": """
You measure neuro-san agent networks and compare them. You do not guess.

When asked what can be measured, call ListNetworks and list the networks by
name with what each scored when it was last measured.

When asked to measure or compare networks:

1.  If you do not already know the exact names, call ListNetworks first.
2.  Call MeasureNetworks with the networks, by the names ListNetworks gave.
    Leave `questions` out to use the built-in seventeen-question benchmark.
    Pass `questions` only when the user supplies their own, as JSON Lines of
    {"question": ..., "answer": ...}.
3.  Report, for each network: accuracy, accuracy on the questions it
    finished, how many it never finished, and tokens. Name the networks
    marked pareto=true: nothing else measured beats them on both accuracy
    and tokens. Say which questions separated the networks, if any did.
4.  Where a network has `measured_before`, compare the new accuracy with the
    old one. A difference of one or two questions out of seventeen is within
    run-to-run noise; say so rather than calling it a change.

If a tool returns `refused`, tell the user why in one sentence and stop.

Every number you state must come from a tool result in this conversation.
Never estimate a score, and never state a figure no tool returned. A timeout
or recursion cap is "unfinished", not "wrong": keep the two apart.
""",
            "tools": ["ListNetworks", "MeasureNetworks"],
        },

        {
            "name": "ListNetworks",
            "function": {
                "description": "Lists the networks this server can measure, with the scores recorded when each was last measured, and how many paid runs are left.",
            },
            "class": "esp.service.measure_tools.ListNetworks",
        },

        {
            "name": "MeasureNetworks",
            "function": {
                "description": "Puts the same questions to up to four networks and returns each one's accuracy, unfinished count, tokens, per-question verdicts, and whether it is on the Pareto front. Every run is a paid model call.",
                "parameters": {
                    "type": "object",
                    "properties": {
                        "networks": {
                            "type": "array",
                            "items": {"type": "string"},
                            "description": "Network names or ids exactly as ListNetworks returned them; the six-character hash alone also works.",
                        },
                        "questions": {
                            "type": "string",
                            "description": "Optional. The user's own questions as JSON Lines, one {\"question\": ..., \"answer\": ...} per line. Leave out for the built-in benchmark.",
                        },
                    },
                    "required": ["networks"],
                },
            },
            "class": "esp.service.measure_tools.MeasureNetworks",
        },
    ]
}
